        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Willow Vale, Mittagong, Braemar, Balaclava, Southern Highlands, New South Wales, Australia\n- Organizations: Wingecarribee Shire\n- Topics: wineries, wine region, cellar doors\n\nFacts:\n- Willow Vale is a northern village in the Southern Highlands of New South Wales, Australia, within Wingecarribee Shire.\n- Willow Vale is located 1 km north of Mittagong.\n- Willow Vale is often considered part of Braemar together with its neighbour Balaclava.\n- Mittagong is home to many wineries in the Southern Highlands.\n- The Southern Highlands has recently grown as a wine and cellar door region.",
